{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-77157",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270613/assets/8b1f250cbc03c9daf6126171c4f7cc70563123c4dba8b7879fdfaf905538f9b8.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{6}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =18+36+36 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{90}=3\\sqrt{10}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
